  "title": "Lok Sabha Prorogation Delay and Constitutional Bill Concerns",
  "summary": "Congress leader Jairam Ramesh and the Hindu National report that the Lok Sabha has not been prorogued after being adjourned sine die, highlighting concerns about the constitutional amendment Bill for delimitation. The Government’s prorogation request was met with criticism, and there is speculation about the government’s intent to pass legislation on women’s reservation.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Jairam Ramesh asks if the delay is due to the Home Minister trying to cobble together numbers for a constitutional amendment Bill for delimitation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Lok Sabha was adjourned sine die in the Monsoon Session on August 13, but there is no formal prorogation yet.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government has not prorogued the session, leading to speculation about its intent to pass a key legislation on women’s reservation law before the 2029 parliamentary polls.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
